# Regenerable intermediates: the nearest-region lookup (66 MB), the base map
# raster and the land mask. `python maps/build_basemap.py` rebuilds them from
# source/ and the climatology in about 25 seconds, and the region lookup is
# cached across runs. Nothing here is a result.
build/

# Rendered frames: one UUID-named directory per state of the world, tens of MB
# apiece and regenerable by maps/snapshot.py for as long as the inputs the frame
# names still exist. data/<build>/INDEX.json is NOT ignored -- frame ids are
# UUIDs, so it is the only record of what each frame was once the pixels are
# gone, and a NEW build's index has to be committable too. Same
# exclude-the-bulk-keep-the-record rule as exoplasim/runs/.
#
# No trailing slash, so this matches the symlink a worktree carries in place of
# a frame as well as the directory itself. The root .gitignore's worktree block
# exists because rules that end in "/" miss those links, and `git add -A` in a
# worktree then commits an absolute path that means nothing anywhere else.
data/*/*
!data/*/INDEX.json
